# spec-kit ships the /speckit-* skills into .claude/skills/, and those are shared
# tooling that MUST be committed. A user-level core.excludesFile commonly ignores
# `**/.claude/` wholesale; a repo .gitignore outranks it, so re-include the directory
# here. Git cannot re-include a path under an excluded DIRECTORY — hence `.claude/*`
# with a star rather than a trailing slash, or no negation below it can ever fire.
#
# Allowlist, not denylist: everything under .claude/ is ignored and skills/ is named
# back in. Tools keep inventing new session state in there (settings.local.json,
# scheduled_tasks.lock, ...) and an enumeration would leak the next one into a commit.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# spec-kit session state: create-new-feature.sh writes .specify/feature.json on nearly
# every /speckit-* invocation. Committing it hands every contributor someone else's
# current-feature pointer. Everything else under .specify/ is shared infrastructure
# and IS committed.
.specify/feature.json
.specify/extensions.yml
